let's speak now to dr kathy gardner who  lost her father michael at the peak of  the pandemic spring 2020 are very sorry  for your loss thousands of families  will sense will have a sense of justice  and a sense of relief tell me how you're  feeling right now dr gardner oh huge  huge relief we knew at the time that  something had gone  so badly wrong i've known all along that  what the government did was wrong and  and today it's that vindication that  that we were right and i'm  so pleased that that's that's been  proven yeah what sort of messages of  support have you had throughout  this this  case and bringing it to the high court  you were forced to do that because you  wanted the government to be held  accountable do you feel now that they  are being held to account and that this  will change the course of future  pandemics and and possibly open  the doors to thousands of compensation  claims as well  that's there's quite a lot of questions  there i've had  fantastic support from from so many  families in a similar situation to mine  and that support has been invaluable and  indeed i wouldn't be here today had it  not been for the funding that that so  many thousands of people supported i'm  so grateful for that and this is the  vindication that we were right all along  i was right to bring the case  i was so determined to try and hold the  government to account this was such a  huge failing and i was insulted every  time they've said oh we did everything  we could and it was unprecedented and  and  no you didn't do everything you could  and no it wasn't unprecedented  and one of my main aims  was well was to make sure this never  happens again that if we're ever in this  situation again that the government will  have to make sure that they take  everything they should into account to  make sure they do whatever they can to  protect the most vulnerable people in  society when you were at home  [Music]  i imagine you weren't allowed to attend  your father's funeral but  when you were there you were mourning  for your father and you heard the  government responses  time and time again that they've thrown  a shield around care homes to protect  elderly and vulnerable  residents  how did that make you feel  i was disgusted i've been disgusted by  by the constant denial that anything was  done wrong the constant claims that they  handled the pandemic so well you know  we've had a massive death toll in this  country the top the death toll in care  homes at the start was was unbelievable  i think somewhere near half the deaths  in the first few months were care home  residents the very group of people that  should have been the most  protected by that and of course grieving  during the height of the pandemic when  we were in lockdown  was very difficult i couldn't be with my  father when he died i couldn't hold his  hand all those things that you think  will be  what you would normally expect to do  when you're losing a parent  there were three of us at his funeral  myself my husband and my mother that was  all no other family and friends at all  but all the families that have gone  through this have really been  traumatized by by losses during a  pandemic  and when you have a deep belief that the  government itself has let you down  that they've taken steps they absolutely  shouldn't have taken that's made it even  more  painful  and the constant to say the constant  denial and the constant  saying we did so well just is  is insulting  we haven't had a government response  to the judgment yet  did you ever believe that the government  had acted in the interests of the  country because it was dealing with an  unprecedented health crisis was there a  part of you before  michael died that  do you believe that the government was  trying to do its best if not actually  doing it was it actually trying to do  its best if you think  i didn't have a sense of that at the  beginning i think i  you have to remember my father died on  the third of april 2020 he got ill in  march so very very early on in in the  pandemic that we were as we were aware  of it  i think i hoped the government would do  a good job we used to have a very very  good public health system in this  country  i thought at the time in the early  months of 2020  surely we won't suffer as badly as italy  was suffering in those early days if we  remember that  but  when i realized that my father  had covered or  apparently had coveted  he was never tested  um i couldn't believe it  and then when i heard about the hospital  discharge policy and i looked it up and  i read it i couldn't believe it  that there was no mention anywhere of  how care home residents should be  protected so myself and my neighbours  were all sheltering at home keeping  ourselves safe  my father was in just a larger home  exposed completely exposed  what do you want to see happen  next we haven't had a government  response this will set a future for  further  health emergencies in the  future and  this is the first time the government  has been held accountable  pre-inquiry before any inquiry what  would you like to see happen next  well  i  have asked for an apology  from matt hancock who was secretary of  state at the time  although to me an apology is you know  it's all very well but actually i think  he also should consider his position as  an mp he's still an mp  he stood up in parliament and said to  mps that he tried to put a protective  ring around care homes i knew that was a  lie when it was said first of all in  spring 2020 and it's definitely a lie  and i think he should consider that the  prime minister absolutely should go but  i don't believe he has any conscience or  moral fibre that says that he should  take any responsibility for this but as  far as i'm concerned he absolutely does  this was under his watch
 

